// Golden vectors, determinism, resume, the stage entry point and the
// pipeline of the resources stage (spec P1-05 sections 2, 3, 5 R7, 6
// invariant 6, 10.3 and 10.4; P1-00 sections 3, 10.1 and 14 X1, X2; D10).
//
// The golden vectors in worldgen/tests/golden/p1-05-resources.txt were
// generated by worldgen/tests/reference/p1_resources_reference.py, the test
// writer's exact-integer reference written from the spec alone, on input
// layers checked against p1-04-biomes.txt. Each case's seven inputs are
// recomputed by the earlier stages and compared first, so an upstream
// change shows as such. The items are then compared in step order, so a
// failure names the first step that diverges: drainage height (the shared
// G7 seam with k = 1), slope (the test's own G8), the two distances (seam
// chamfer_metres), the ore noise (the test's own fbm2 and seam
// resource_ore_noise), the seven layers (seam resources_layers, checked cell
// by cell against the test's own R3 to R6), the walk-area counts, the
// branch coverage and the report values.
//
// The N >= 512 cases run in the suite "resources-slow":
//   worldgen-tests -ts=resources-slow --no-skip

